'''zinco''' (zing′kō), ''v. i.'' [< ''zinco'', ''n.''] To etch with acid a zinc plate containing on its surface a design intended for printing by typographic methods. [Eng.]

{{smaller block|Drawings Wanted (on litho paper for ''zincoing'') for a Provincial Journal. {{right|''Athenæum'', No. 3235, p. 591.}}}}

'''zincode''' (zing′kōd), ''n.'' [< NL. ''zincum'', zinc, + Gr. ὁδός, way (cf. ''anode'', ''cathode'').] The negative pole of a voltaic battery; the anode of an electrolytic cell.

'''zincograph''' (zing′kọ-grȧf), ''n.'' [See ''zincography''.] A plate or a picture produced by zincography. Also ''zincotype''.

{{smaller block|Reproduced in ''zincograph'' by the aid of photography. {{right|''Edinburgh Rev.'', CXLV. 231.}}}}

